  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「シロバナムシヨケギク」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%B7%E3%83%AD%E3%83%90%E3%83%8A%E3%83%A0%E3%82%B7%E3%83%A8%E3%82%B1%E3%82%AE%E3%82%AF",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 110990450,
      "text": "シロバナムシヨケギク は、キク科の多年草である。胚珠の部分に殺虫成分のピレトリンを含むため、除虫菊（ジョチュウギク）の名前でも知られ殺虫剤の原料に使用されてきた。原産地は地中海沿岸であり、セルビアで発見された。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Tanacetum cinerariifolium」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanacetum_cinerariifolium",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1352115956,
      "text": "Tanacetum cinerariifolium is a species of flowering plant in the aster family, Asteraceae, and formerly part of the genus Pyrethrum, but now placed in the genus Chrysanthemum, or the genus Tanacetum by some biologists. It is called the Dalmatian chrysanthemum or Dalmatian pyrethrum, denoting its origin in western coastal Balkan Peninsula, where it ranges from Dalmatia to Albania. It looks more like the common daisy than other pyrethrums do. Its flowers, typically white with yellow centers, grow from numerous fairly rigid stems. Plants have blue-green leaves and grow to 45 to 100 cm in height."
    }
  },
